Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: hfi_cmds: drop H264 8x8 transform property on HFI 1xx/3xx

Bug
---
venc_set_properties() (venc.c) sends HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8
unconditionally when the capture format is V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264. Packetization for
that property only exists in pkt_session_set_property_4xx(); the HFI 3xx
packetizer falls through to pkt_session_set_property_1x(), which has no case
for the property and hits "default: return -EINVAL". The error propagates out
of venc_set_properties() -> venc_start_streaming(), so VIDIOC_REQBUFS fails
with -EINVAL on every HFI 1xx/3xx Venus. Observed on msm8917/ugglite: kretprobe
showed venc_set_properties+0x1a4 == -22 (-EINVAL).

Upstream
--------
Known upstream bug, reported on APQ8016/msm8916 (HFI 1xx):
  https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/5D1EB136-0839-44BF-9F9B-A937237C9C96@noisolation.com/
The subsystem maintainer (Stanimir Varbanov) rejected a venc.c version check and
proposed exactly this one-line change in the packetization layer:
  https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/5a851116-561f-2d00-1310-2debc43ce249@gmail.com/
and asked for a v2 with that change:
  https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/bd5a5b80-6849-bd98-0815-cc94badbec13@gmail.com/
Qualcomm confirmed that on older HFI the video firmware applies 8x8 transform
automatically for High/Constrained High profiles; the property exists only to
let V4+ clients disable it, so dropping it on 1xx/3xx keeps firmware default
behavior (8x8 enabled):
  https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/219b2cf5-4218-2e5c-2f12-718d5554b2b7@quicinc.com/
Same class of fix as the merged commit "media: venus: hfi_cmds: List HDR10
property as unsupported for v1 and v3": HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_HDR10_PQ_SEI
already sits one line above in the same switch. The v2 never landed; mainline
v7.x still sends the property unconditionally (checked 2026-11-15: the tree's
hfi_cmds.c is byte-identical to mainline), hence this local patch.

Mechanism
---------
hfi_venus.c:venus_session_set_property() converts -ENOTSUPP into "return 0"
without writing the HFI packet, so the property is silently skipped instead of
failing the session. HFI 4xx/6xx keep their own case in
pkt_session_set_property_4xx() and still send the property.

Fixes: bfee75f73c37 ("media: venus: venc: add support for V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_8X8_TRANSFORM control")

Apply (from the top of the kernel tree):
  patch -p1 --dry-run < patches/kernel/0003-venus-hfi3xx-skip-h264-8x8-transform.patch
  patch -p1           < patches/kernel/0003-venus-hfi3xx-skip-h264-8x8-transform.patch
  make ARCH=arm64 LLVM=1 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/
Revert:
  patch -p1 -R        < patches/kernel/0003-venus-hfi3xx-skip-h264-8x8-transform.patch

Background: docs/venus.md.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
@@ -1065,6 +1065,7 @@
 		break;
 	}
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_HDR10_PQ_SEI:
+	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8:
 		return -ENOTSUPP;
 
 	/* FOLLOWING PROPERTIES ARE NOT IMPLEMENTED IN CORE YET */
